      <div type="clause" n="3.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:WiLad">Wl lad</ref> 3.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="484" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif se Englisca beclypað Frencisne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#WiLad_3-1.lnote.oe.b"/> mid utlagan þingan ⁊ wille hit þonne on hi<hi rend="italic">m</hi> gesoðian, se Fræncisca bewerie hine mid orneste.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="484" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si Anglicus appellet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#WiLad_3-1.lnote.oe.7"/> Francigenam de utlagaria<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#WiLad_3-1.lnote.oe.8"/> et hoc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#WiLad_3-1.lnote.oe.9"/> super eum inueritare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#WiLad_3-1.lnote.oe.10"/> uelit, defendat se Francigena per bellum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="232" ed="#robertson"/>7 gif se Englisca beclypað Frencisne mid utlagan þingan 7 wille hit þonne on him gesoðian, se Fræncisca bewerie hine mid orneste.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="484" ed="#liebermann"/>3, 1. Und wenn [andererseits] der Englische einen Französischen wegen friedlos<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#WiLad_3-1.lnote.de.1"/> machender Sachen verklagt und dies nun gegen ihn beweisen will, vertheidige sich der Französische durch gerichtlichen Zweikampf.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">3, 1. And if [on the other hand] the Englishman accuses a Frenchman of matters entailing outlawry and wishes now to prove this against him, the Frenchman shall defend himself by judicial combat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="233" ed="#robertson"/>And if the Englishman brings a charge involving outlawry against a Frenchman, and desires further to prove it against him, the Frenchman shall defend himself by combat.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="484"><ref target="clause:WlArt_6-3">Wl art 6.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">6, 3</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:WlArt_6-3">Wl art 6.3</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 232–233 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 484, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WiLad_3-1.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">484</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Wilisman <hi rend="italic">Norðleod</hi> 7; srift <hi rend="italic">II Cn.</hi> 44 <hi rend="italic">Hs. A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. Wilisman Norðleod 7; srift II Cn. 44 MS A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WiLad_3-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">484</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lat <hi rend="italic">M Hk Cs</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lat M Hk Cs</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WiLad_3-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">484</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">utleg. <hi rend="italic">M Hk;</hi> uthl. <hi rend="italic">Cs</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">utleg. M Hk; uthl. Cs</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WiLad_3-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">484</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hec <hi rend="italic">Sc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hec Sc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WiLad_3-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">484</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in ueritate <hi rend="italic">K Cs</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in ueritate K Cs</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="WiLad_3-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">273</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 1, 1{1}</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 1, 1{1}</seg></note>
      </div>
